  <main>
    <section class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">Meet Roy</div><h1>Practical, independent, community-first.</h1><p class="lead">This page is a first-draft campaign bio. It should be refined with Roy’s final candidacy details, family/community background, and official nomination language.</p></section>
    <section class="content">
      <p>Roy Li is running to bring clearer representation, stronger accountability, and practical decision-making to Richmond City Hall.</p>
      <p>His campaign is built around a simple belief: residents should not feel that civic politics is something happening far away from them. City Hall affects taxes, traffic, safety, housing, business permits, parks, and the basic rhythm of daily life. People deserve a representative who treats those concerns as urgent and real.</p>
      <h2>Why Roy is running</h2>
      <p>Richmond is a city of families, immigrants, entrepreneurs, seniors, young people, homeowners, renters, and workers. Too many residents feel seen during elections but forgotten during decisions. This campaign is about turning representation into power residents can actually feel.</p>
      <h2>The campaign promise</h2>
      <p>Listen first. Speak clearly. Spend carefully. Govern openly. Deliver practically.</p>
    </section>
